;;; Mini CMUdict fixture. Same format as the real dictionary (BSD-2-Clause):
;;; WORD  P1 P2 P3, two spaces before the phonemes; WORD(n) for alternates.
;;; Every entry here backs a row in the verdict table or the guardrail table.
ATE  EY1 T
EIGHT  EY1 T
LATE  L EY1 T
COLLATE  K AH0 L EY1 T
IMPREGNATE  IH0 M P R EH1 G N EY2 T
ADJUDICATE  AH0 JH UW1 D IH0 K EY2 T
DEFENESTRATE  D IH0 F EH1 N AH0 S T R EY2 T
OBJURGATE  AA1 B JH ER0 G EY2 T
CHOCOLATE  CH AO1 K L AH0 T
COMMENSURATE  K AH0 M EH1 N S ER0 AH0 T
HAT  HH AE1 T
SATE  S EY1 T
READ  R IY1 D
READ(1)  R EH1 D
BED  B EH1 D
TEAR  T IH1 R
TEAR(1)  T EH1 R
BEER  B IH1 R
CARE  K EH1 R
KATE  K EY1 T
GATE  G EY1 T
GATES  G EY1 T S
PLATES  P L EY1 T S
;;; The `-ate` guardrails: an unstressed schwa in the final syllable, which no
;;; normalisation may erase (see docs/adr/0010, and CHOCOLATE/COMMENSURATE above).
PRIVATE  P R AY1 V AH0 T
CLIMATE  K L AY1 M AH0 T
SENATE  S EH1 N AH0 T
ACCURATE  AE1 K Y ER0 AH0 T
;;; The cot-caught merger: AO words that must join their AA counterparts.
DOCKED  D AA1 K T
TALKED  T AO1 K T
WALKED  W AO1 K T
BALKED  B AO1 K T
STALKED  S T AO1 K T
HAWKED  HH AO1 K T
;;; Pre-lateral position is merged too — `ball` rhymes with `doll`.
BALL  B AO1 L
DOLL  D AA1 L
;;; Pre-rhotic position is not merged. These three pairs are the guardrail.
FOR  F AO1 R
FAR  F AA1 R
BORN  B AO1 R N
BARN  B AA1 R N
CORD  K AO1 R D
CARD  K AA1 R D
;;; Syllabic consonants: the schwa before a word-final L/N/M is optional in
;;; ordinary speech, so `gruel` is heard as a rhyme for `cool` (ADR-0010).
COOL  K UW1 L
POOL  P UW1 L
GRUEL  G R UW1 AH0 L
DUEL  D UW1 AH0 L
CREWEL  K R UW1 AH0 L
RENEWAL  R IH0 N UW1 AH0 L
;;; A full unstressed vowel is not a schwa and is never dropped: `crayon` must
;;; not become `crane`.
CRANE  K R EY1 N
CRAYON  K R EY1 AA0 N
;;; Suffix derivation (issue #77): the stems the build composes the five words
;;; the issue names from, each paired with a stem whose derived form rhymes, so
;;; the derived reading can be adjudicated rather than merely inspected. Every
;;; suffixed form is deliberately absent — that is what makes it a target.
ABOLISH  AH0 B AA1 L IH0 SH
POLISH  P AA1 L IH0 SH
YOUTHFUL  Y UW1 TH F AH0 L
TRUTHFUL  T R UW1 TH F AH0 L
ZESTFUL  Z EH1 S T F AH0 L
RESTFUL  R EH1 S T F AH0 L
ABASH  AH0 B AE1 SH
ABASHED  AH0 B AE1 SH T
UNABASHED  AH2 N AH0 B AE1 SH T
# `unabashedly` is carried with the reading CMUdict actually gives it, so the
# `abashedly` assertion is anchored to the dictionary rather than to a second
# derivation making the same mistake. Its syllabic `IH0 D` is the whole point.
UNABASHEDLY  AH2 N AH0 B AE1 SH IH0 D L IY0
# `cuss`/`justly` pin the false accept the participle route produced: composing
# `-ly` onto `cussed` (`K AH1 S T`) lands `cussedly` in the `justly` family.
CUSS  K AH1 S
JUSTLY  JH AH1 S T L IY0
YODEL  Y OW1 D AH0 L
